From d3962cd5122dd48c6b9c01581b432bd6abdcbff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:03:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the seat's head blinks on the minimap; the menu never
 pauses online; SRNP_PATCH

- Minimap (task 0x80414758): every racer's head is drawn, from last
  place to first; a player's head (racer index +0x1029 below the player
  count) blinks, the others are fixed. On a 1P machine that was racer 0
  on every machine. The index it reads (0x80415C54) now goes through
  three words of code in free low memory (0x80002E00: lbz, addi -seat,
  blr), so the seat's racer is the one that blinks. Set with the HUD
  (SRNP_HUD=0 leaves it).
- The runner's menu opens as in Netplay when SRNP_RELAY is set: the
  match goes on behind it (srnp::RelayConfigured()).
- SRNP_PATCH=<address>=<word>,...: code words written for the race and
  taken back at its end, for experiments.

Measured: camera and HUD on racer 5, the same frames: racer 5's head
blinks instead of racer 0's. 8 runners on one PC, each with its own
seat's HUD, a full race: 142 checksums equal, 0 divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
